    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50757" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĕtĕrīnārĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		veterinus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to beasts of
				burden and draught.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">medicina,</span>”
				<i>farriery</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					7, 3, 16</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĕtĕrīnārĭus</span></b> ,
				ii, m., <i>a
				cattle-doctor</i>, <i>farrier</i>, <i>veterinarian</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 6, 8,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 5, 14</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">11, 1,
			12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĕtĕ-rīnārĭum</span></b> ,
				ii, n., <i>a place for
				taking care of diseased animals</i>, <i><span class="en">Hyg.
				Grom. p. 12</span></i>.</div>
